    "q-95068": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95068",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+t\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$",
      "worked_solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,j)\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t}+t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95068-a",
